{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"ff91daa7-3671-428b-aa4a-741e289da74b\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"According to NCERT, what principle was intended to guide relations between the Centre and the States in India?\",\"hi\":\"NCERT के अनुसार भारत में केंद्र और राज्यों के संबंधों का मार्गदर्शन किस सिद्धांत से होना था?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Permanent confrontation\",\"hi\":\"स्थायी टकराव\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Cooperation while recognising diversity and emphasising unity\",\"hi\":\"विविधता को मान्यता देते हुए और एकता पर बल देते हुए सहयोग\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Complete dependence of States on local bodies\",\"hi\":\"राज्यों की स्थानीय निकायों पर पूर्ण निर्भरता\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Separate international sovereignty for every State\",\"hi\":\"हर राज्य की अलग अंतरराष्ट्रीय संप्रभुता\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 7, Federalism, 2026-27 reprint, printed pp. 156, 158, 164 and 172. Direct official document: NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 7 (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps207.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ff33036c-979d-4033-b598-42e0370f5720\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"If difficulty arises in construing part of the Hindi translation under Article 394A, what does the Constitution require?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 394A के अधीन हिंदी अनुवाद के किसी भाग को समझने में कठिनाई उत्पन्न हो तो संविधान क्या अपेक्षा करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The translation automatically becomes void\",\"hi\":\"अनुवाद स्वतः शून्य हो जाता है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The President must cause it to be suitably revised\",\"hi\":\"राष्ट्रपति उसका उपयुक्त पुनरीक्षण कराएँगे\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The Supreme Court must rewrite the entire Constitution\",\"hi\":\"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय पूरे संविधान को पुनः लिखेगा\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Only Parliament may publish an unofficial summary\",\"hi\":\"केवल संसद अनौपचारिक सार प्रकाशित कर सकती है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026, Article 394A(2)-(3) (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ff03fac8-d64e-4c99-9dc0-73c97cb83088\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which list consists entirely of liberties expressly named in the Preamble?\",\"hi\":\"कौन-सी सूची पूरी तरह उन स्वतंत्रताओं से बनी है जिनका उद्देशिका में स्पष्ट उल्लेख है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Trade, movement, residence and profession\",\"hi\":\"व्यापार, संचरण, निवास और व्यवसाय\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Property, contract, inheritance and taxation\",\"hi\":\"संपत्ति, संविदा, उत्तराधिकार और कराधान\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Press, association, assembly and petition\",\"hi\":\"प्रेस, संगठन, सभा और याचिका\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Thought, expression, belief, faith and worship\",\"hi\":\"विचार, अभिव्यक्ति, विश्वास, धर्म और उपासना\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Preamble and Articles 19 and 25. Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"febfe1c4-0b99-487a-bacb-0d0808a08473\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"The Union, State and Concurrent Lists are contained in which part of the constitutional scheme?\",\"hi\":\"संघ, राज्य और समवर्ती सूचियाँ संवैधानिक व्यवस्था के किस भाग में दी गई हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The Fifth Schedule alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल पाँचवीं अनुसूची\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The Seventh Schedule read with Article 246\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 246 के साथ पठित सातवीं अनुसूची\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The Tenth Schedule read with Article 102\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 102 के साथ पठित दसवीं अनुसूची\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The Preamble alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल प्रस्तावना\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 246, PDF p. 175, and Seventh Schedule, Lists I-III, PDF pp. 340-353. Direct official document: Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fe6278f4-0108-4978-97ab-e3a2037bc847\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"According to the verified NCERT source table, Law-making procedure is associated with which source?\",\"hi\":\"सत्यापित NCERT स्रोत-सारणी के अनुसार विधि-निर्माण प्रक्रिया किस स्रोत से संबंधित है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Irish Constitution\",\"hi\":\"आयरिश संविधान\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"British Constitution\",\"hi\":\"ब्रिटिश संविधान\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"French Constitution\",\"hi\":\"फ्रांसीसी संविधान\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Canadian Constitution\",\"hi\":\"कनाडाई संविधान\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: NCERT Class XI, source table, printed p. 22; Constitution of India, relevant provisions. | Direct official documents: NCERT, Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 1 “Constitution: Why and How?”, Reprint 2026-27 — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps201.pdf ; Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India, as on 1 May 2026 — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf | Verification date: 2026-07-13 | Confidence: high.\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fd829549-ad85-46c2-8d26-02bc21786651\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"The Supreme Court’s discretionary power to grant special leave to appeal is found in:\",\"hi\":\"अपील की विशेष अनुमति देने की सर्वोच्च न्यायालय की विवेकाधीन शक्ति किसमें है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Article 136\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 136\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Article 129\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 129\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Article 143\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 143\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Article 214\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 214\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 136(1)-(2). Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fb557157-579a-40c0-95e8-1c20331e66f0\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which preserved record explains the reasoning behind constitutional provisions and assists interpretation?\",\"hi\":\"कौन-सा संरक्षित अभिलेख संवैधानिक प्रावधानों के पीछे का तर्क बताता और व्याख्या में सहायता करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Supreme Court Reports\",\"hi\":\"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय रिपोर्ट्स\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Cabinet Mission Statement\",\"hi\":\"कैबिनेट मिशन वक्तव्य\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Government of India Act, 1935 alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल भारत शासन अधिनियम, 1935\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Constituent Assembly Debates\",\"hi\":\"संविधान सभा वाद-विवाद\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: NCERT Class IX, printed p. 25. | Direct official documents: NCERT, Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2 “Constitutional Design”, Reprint 2025-26 — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf ; NCERT, Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 1 “Constitution: Why and How?”, Reprint 2026-27 — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps201.pdf | Verification date: 2026-07-13 | Confidence: high.\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"UPSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fb2a8ec6-3a07-4be6-9aff-845850f00fbd\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 139A allows the Supreme Court, in specified circumstances, to:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 139A निर्दिष्ट परिस्थितियों में सर्वोच्च न्यायालय को क्या करने देता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Withdraw certain cases involving the same or substantially the same questions of law from High Courts and dispose of them itself, and transfer cases between High Courts\",\"hi\":\"समान या पर्याप्त रूप से समान विधि-प्रश्न वाले कुछ मामले उच्च न्यायालयों से वापस लेकर स्वयं निपटाना तथा उच्च न्यायालयों के बीच मामले स्थानांतरित करना\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Appoint all district judges without consultation\",\"hi\":\"बिना परामर्श सभी जिला न्यायाधीश नियुक्त करना\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Abolish the High Courts by judicial order\",\"hi\":\"न्यायिक आदेश से उच्च न्यायालय समाप्त करना\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Create separate State constitutions\",\"hi\":\"अलग राज्य संविधान बनाना\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 139A(1)-(2). Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"faf5f8dc-6130-4c95-ac31-952e49bd88c3\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 7 generally addresses persons who migrated from India to Pakistan after which date?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 7 सामान्यतः उन व्यक्तियों से संबंधित है जो किस तारीख के बाद भारत से पाकिस्तान गए?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"15 August 1947\",\"hi\":\"15 अगस्त 1947\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"1 March 1947\",\"hi\":\"1 मार्च 1947\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"19 July 1948\",\"hi\":\"19 जुलाई 1948\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"26 January 1950\",\"hi\":\"26 जनवरी 1950\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 7, opening words, PDF p. 35. Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fa991b67-35e7-456d-be62-556b7f95ea74\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Assertion (A): A written Constitution can remain a “living document.”\\nReason (R): Its written text may be amended and interpreted while retaining an identifiable constitutional framework.\",\"hi\":\"अभिकथन (A): लिखित संविधान “जीवंत दस्तावेज” बना रह सकता है।\\nकारण (R): पहचान योग्य संवैधानिक ढाँचा बनाए रखते हुए उसके लिखित पाठ में संशोधन और उसकी व्याख्या की जा सकती है।\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A\",\"hi\":\"A और R दोनों सही हैं तथा R, A की सही व्याख्या है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Both A and R are true, but R is not the correct explanation of A\",\"hi\":\"A और R दोनों सही हैं, किंतु R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A is true, but R is false\",\"hi\":\"A सही है, किंतु R गलत है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A is false, but R is true\",\"hi\":\"A गलत है, किंतु R सही है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 9, pp. 196-200 and 212-215 (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps209.pdf); Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026, Contents and amendment footnotes (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"UPSC\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0}],\"nextCursor\":\"fa991b67-35e7-456d-be62-556b7f95ea74\",\"hasMore\":true}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":300,"tags":["question-batch","question-batch:subtopic:v9:0a04beb7-714b-4831-b999-168ca1b24e4e"]}